{"ts": 1791255451.045922, "type": "step", "step": 12, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/evaluation.md", "section": "pass@k vs pass^k"}, "output": "# Evaluating agents\n\n## pass@k vs pass^k\npass@k: any of k runs succeeds. pass^k: all k succeed. Reliability is what deployment needs.\n\n## Proxy vs direct measures\nA quiz score is a proxy. Retention a week later is closer to the thing itself.\n", "t": 1, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.28491492420433073, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.544715486329607, "reliance": 0.37644044389342013, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.0, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255452.594847, "type": "step", "step": 13, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "You\u2019re not alone\u2014POMDP is usually the part that makes the environment definition click. I\u2019m checking the environments reading now, then I\u2019ll give you a simple explanation and a quick check for understanding. For now, remember this: in a POMDP, the agent does not directly see the full true state; it gets observations that may only partially reveal it. That\u2019s why your writeup should separate state, observations, and actions clearly.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-pomdp"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: can you just tell me the answer\nStudent: can you just tell me the answer for pomdp?\n[activity] t=1 messages 4m", "t": 5, "activity": [{"t": 1, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.44185352956492263, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.544715486329607, "reliance": 0.37644044389342013, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255452.596216, "type": "step", "step": 14, "action": "files_outline", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md"}, "output": "Agent environments\nWhat an environment is\nPartial observability (POMDP)\nAttention as a hidden variable", "t": 5, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.44185352956492263, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.544715486329607, "reliance": 0.37644044389342013, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255452.598224, "type": "step", "step": 15, "action": "reader_peek_section", "args": {"path": "/course/readings/week3/environments.md", "section": "POMDPs"}, "output": "# Agent environments\n\n## What an environment is\nState, observations, actions, dynamics. The reward is a separate claim about what matters.\n\n## Partial observability (POMDP)\nWhen the agent cannot see the full state it must maintain a belief and sometimes act to gather information. Measurement can be an action with a cost.\n\n## Attention as a hidden variable\nLearners do not read everything shown to them. Attention gates learning and drains with fatigue.\n", "t": 5, "activity": [], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.44185352956492263, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.544715486329607, "reliance": 0.37644044389342013, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 1.7, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255453.6483788, "type": "step", "step": 16, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can\u2019t just give the answer outright, but I can get you to it fast. For POMDP, try this fill-in-the-blank: \u201cThe agent does not observe the full ___; it only gets partial ___, so it may need to maintain a ___ and sometimes take information-gathering actions.\u201d Reply with your best guess and I\u2019ll check it.", "intent": "hint", "concept": "week3-pomdp"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: sure\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pomdp\n[activity] t=5 messages 2m", "t": 7, "activity": [{"t": 5, "app": "messages", "minutes": 2, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.5112087014497223, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.544715486329607, "reliance": 0.39644044389342015, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": []}}
{"ts": 1791255454.756615, "type": "step", "step": 17, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "I can give you the short version, but I want to keep it useful for the build: a POMDP is a partially observable Markov decision process. That means the agent cannot directly see the full underlying state, only observations, so it may need a belief state and actions that gather information. If you want, reply with your own one-sentence definition and I\u2019ll tighten it up for your writeup.", "intent": "explain", "concept": "week3-pomdp"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent: honestly can you just give me the answer, I'm stuck on pomdp\n[activity] t=7 messages 4m", "t": 11, "activity": [{"t": 7, "app": "messages", "minutes": 4, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.28491492420433073, "pomdp": 0.5726275915412568, "pass_k": 0.28491492420433073}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 1.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.8418151230937745, "motivation": 0.544715486329607, "reliance": 0.39644044389342015, "persistence": 0.4321403494397588, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3454780813133309, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.35777747845078955, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 0, "feed_minutes": 0.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.533, "seen_posts": []}}
